{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2311018318609b331491f08efac7058d58e99e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> is between  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24c16d20f53457d1ad81a31d186fd6a1b30730e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 0 \\text{ and } \\frac{1}{10} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{10} \\text{ and } \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\text{ and } \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\text{ and } \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\text{ and } \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"677\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Converting the fractions into decimals, we have:  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01fb3d068028295366b47ad9c19274f247434bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10} = 0.1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba326c9abb040f65c53bf23c0030a967e97afffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} = 0.2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f7d3a81dd4d5cea88f0aaf20ae06196a77802d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} = 0.2500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/8757badb3a3220b80d87a5be3c703a643ea9509e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} = 0.\\overline{3333}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/77104d86dbfa0732a976fc586f90d6a5e7586bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = 0.5000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p><p>From these numbers, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2311018318609b331491f08efac7058d58e99e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/92550b3bffab3298ed192533d0d234a5882f1e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{5} \\text{ and } \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"112\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></t